  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Documents",
      "description": "Upload a PDF to process it with a document type. The API stores the file in the inbox\nbucket, records a document and queues a job; the worker does the rest."
    },
    {
      "name": "Jobs",
      "description": "A job processes one document with one version of a document type. Jobs move through\n`queued`, `running` and then `succeeded`, `awaiting_review`, `needs_review`\n(a processing problem for an operator), `failed` (after retries), `rejected` or\n`cancelled`. See the [job lifecycle](https://github.com/kenhayward/ingestion-harness/blob/main/docs/architecture.md#job-lifecycle)."
    },
    {
      "name": "Review & steps",
      "description": "Jobs of document types with a review policy stop in `awaiting_review`. Reviewers read the\ndraft outputs, record edits, then approve (the edited outputs are published) or reject\n(final). Each extraction step's run can be inspected and re-run."
    },
    {
      "name": "Results",
      "description": "Published outputs, read from the final target bucket: the documents a job delivered, their\nvalues and their files."
    },
    {
      "name": "Specs",
      "description": "Document definitions loaded from the repository's `specs/` folder (legacy `spec.yaml` and\n`template.yaml`). Versions are immutable once published."
    },
    {
      "name": "Templates",
      "description": "Document types kept in the database: drafts are editable, published versions are immutable.\nTemplates import and export as YAML. See\n[ADR 0003](https://github.com/kenhayward/ingestion-harness/blob/main/docs/adr/0003-versioned-document-specs.md)."
    },
    {
      "name": "References & regression",
      "description": "References are verified output values for a sample PDF. Regression runs process the\nreferences' PDFs with a template version and score the outputs against them; metrics\nsummarise a document type's runs."
    },
    {
      "name": "Models",
      "description": "Language models the worker discovered from the configured providers. Model refs are\n`provider/model-id` or an alias such as `default` or `fast`."
    },
    {
      "name": "Projects & data policy",
      "description": "The Workbench builds a document type from sample PDFs, one project per type (the project id\nis the template id). A project's data policy decides whether its documents may be sent to\nexternal model providers (`external`) or only to local ones (`local`). See\n[ADR 0007](https://github.com/kenhayward/ingestion-harness/blob/main/docs/adr/0007-workbench.md) and the\n[Workbench design](https://github.com/kenhayward/ingestion-harness/blob/main/docs/design/workbench.md)."
    },
    {
      "name": "Samples & brief",
      "description": "Samples are the project's PDFs, each in the **dev** set (seen by drafting) or the\n**holdout** set (used only to score). Uploading a sample prepares its text (with OCR where\nneeded). The brief describes what the document type must extract."
    },
    {
      "name": "Drafting stages & proposals",
      "description": "A drafting model proposes the template in stages (survey, outputs, sections, steps), each a\nset of typed changes the user accepts in full or in part. Anchor previews check section\nanchors against the dev samples."
    },
    {
      "name": "Test runs",
      "description": "Test runs process samples with the open draft. They are never delivered to the target."
    },
    {
      "name": "Evaluation, iterations & comparisons",
      "description": "An evaluation runs the draft over a sample set and scores the outputs against the\nreferences; each evaluation is recorded as an iteration with a snapshot of the definition.\nComparisons run several models over the same samples."
    },
    {
      "name": "Feedback & revise",
      "description": "Feedback notes on dev samples and iterations, and the **revise** stage, which proposes\nchanges from the open feedback and the latest evaluation failures."
    },
    {
      "name": "Holdout & publish gate",
      "description": "Holdout reference runs and the publish gate: a version is published only when its newest\nholdout evaluation covers every ready holdout sample and scores at or above the project's\nthreshold, unless an override reason is given."
    },
    {
      "name": "Bundles",
      "description": "Export a project as a zip bundle (samples, prepared text, brief, draft and drafting\ncontext) and import one as a new project."
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth & sessions",
      "description": "Sign in with an access token to get a session cookie (`ih_session`). Every `/api` route\nneeds the session except sign-in, sign-out and these docs. See\n[ADR 0006](https://github.com/kenhayward/ingestion-harness/blob/main/docs/adr/0006-token-access.md)."
    },
    {
      "name": "Access tokens",
      "description": "Admins issue and revoke the access tokens people sign in with. The admin token itself\nrotates on every API start and is printed in the API log."
    },
    {
      "name": "Data-lake S3 keys",
      "description": "Read-only S3 credentials for data-lake consumers of the publish bucket. Secrets are shown\nonce. See [ADR 0008](https://github.com/kenhayward/ingestion-harness/blob/main/docs/adr/0008-s3-read-keys.md)."
    },
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "description": "Liveness and readiness checks for load balancers and orchestrators. They need no session."
    }
  ],
